(Stage 1d — a function returning `a value` carries its runtime tag back in
 r11; appending such a result to a list forwards the tag, so a later
 predicate on the appended slot classifies it correctly. Acceptance 2.)

To passthrough with a value called v. Return a value, v.

a list called m is [1, "two", 3.5].
a list called out is [].
For each item in m,
  append passthrough of item to out.
For each o in out,
  if o is a number, print "N",
  otherwise if o is a text, print "T",
  otherwise print "D".